<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Crater Lake Rim Trail (Rim Village clockwise to Park Headquarters)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:313-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="42.911007" lon="-122.146077"><ele>2171.0</ele><name>Rim Village</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:rim-village (OSM parking way/151972388); confidence: high; pdf_page: 315; book_elev_ft: 7000; quote: The normal direction to ski the rim is clockwise, starting at Rim Village rather than at Park Headquarters.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.945793" lon="-122.168713"><ele>2323.4</ele><name>Watchman Overlook</name><desc>source: OSM viewpoint node/540927931 on West Rim Drive, north of the saddle below The Watchman; confidence: high; pdf_page: 311; quote: ski to the 7,172-foot saddle between Discovery Point and The Watchman, almost 3 miles from Rim Village</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.979716" lon="-122.083354"><ele>2079.6</ele><name>Cleetwood Cove Trailhead</name><desc>source: OSM trailhead node/13121587998 on the north side of Rim Drive; confidence: high; pdf_page: 315; quote: The northeast side of the loop is the most demanding in terms of route finding.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.914091" lon="-122.071402"><ele>2058.6</ele><name>Kerr Notch</name><desc>source: OSM viewpoint node/2315614413 on East Rim Drive; confidence: high; pdf_page: 312; book_elev_ft: 6753</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.910530" lon="-122.072620"><ele>2033.6</ele><name>Dutton Cliffs bypass leaves Rim Drive</name><desc>source: NPS Crater Lake avalanche bypass handout, rev 11/2010 (https://www.nps.gov/crla/planyourvisit/upload/2010-avalanche-bypass-handout-508-2.pdf): Kerr Notch &amp; Dutton Cliffs panel, where the bypass route branches south-east off the road below Kerr Notch, by affine fit to OSM; confidence: medium</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.901746" lon="-122.060120"><ele>1954.3</ele><name>Dutton Cliffs bypass meets Pinnacles road</name><desc>source: NPS Crater Lake avalanche bypass handout, rev 11/2010 (https://www.nps.gov/crla/planyourvisit/upload/2010-avalanche-bypass-handout-508-2.pdf): the bypass route meets the Pinnacles route; OSM node/4008621560 on the Pinnacles road, 120 m from the fitted point; confidence: medium</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.879891" lon="-122.037864"><ele>1823.0</ele><name>Lost Creek (Pinnacles road / Grayback Drive)</name><desc>source: OSM start of Grayback Drive way/1213731900 off the Pinnacles road at Lost Creek; confidence: high; pdf_page: 314; quote: then drops to Lost Creek ... From here the bypass route climbs 800 feet up the valley on the Pinnacles road 3 miles to Kerr Notch. The bypass route is 2.7 miles longer than following the Rim Road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.882042" lon="-122.097348"><ele>1985.3</ele><name>Grayback road / Vidae Ridge bypass trail</name><desc>source: OSM north end of Crater Peak Trail way/652150449 on the Grayback road below Vidae Falls; handout Sun Notch &amp; Vidae Ridge panel: the Vidae Ridge Avalanche Bypass Trail leaves the Greyback Trail here; confidence: medium</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.876898" lon="-122.103593"><ele>2018.7</ele><name>Vidae Ridge bypass trail back at Rim Drive</name><desc>source: OSM Crater Peak Trail way/652150449 where it passes 28 m from the Rim Drive bend (the handout's Crater Peak trail junction, the book's 6,654 ft bend); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 313</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.896827" lon="-122.133714"><ele>1973.4</ele><name>Park Headquarters</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:crater-lake-park-headquarters (OSM parking way/208653507); confidence: high; pdf_page: 315; book_elev_ft: 6475; quote: In this direction you will end your tour at Park Headquarters, 625 feet lower than the rim.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Crater Lake Rim Trail (Rim Village clockwise to Park Headquarters)</name><desc>1. Rim Village -&gt; Watchman Overlook: osm (high), 4.13 mi | 2. Watchman Overlook -&gt; Cleetwood Cove Trailhead: osm (high), 6.69 mi | 3. Cleetwood Cove Trailhead -&gt; Kerr Notch: osm (high), 10.30 mi | 4. Kerr Notch -&gt; Dutton Cliffs bypass leaves Rim Drive: osm (high), 0.32 mi | 5. Dutton Cliffs bypass leaves Rim Drive -&gt; Dutton Cliffs bypass meets Pinnacles road: line (medium), 0.91 mi | 6. Dutton Cliffs bypass meets Pinnacles road -&gt; Lost Creek (Pinnacles road / Grayback Drive): osm (high), 1.92 mi | 7. Lost Creek (Pinnacles road / Grayback Drive) -&gt; Grayback road / Vidae Ridge bypass trail: osm (high), 4.68 mi | 8. Grayback road / Vidae Ridge bypass trail -&gt; Vidae Ridge bypass trail back at Rim Drive: osm (medium), 0.58 mi | 9. Vidae Ridge bypass trail back at Rim Drive -&gt; Park Headquarters: osm (high), 2.58 mi</desc>
